what do you need to know about marvel's  living vampire before he makes his big  screen debut who's in the cast who's  directing keep watching to find out  everything we know about morbius  morbius was originally set to release in  the summer of 2020 right in the middle  of blockbuster season alongside other  major comic book releases like black  widow and eternals that was a bold  choice but like the rest of the 2020  summer movie season the pandemic got in  the way and sony moved its living  vampire back to the spring of 2021  eventually spring became winter and the  film was bumped up to its current  release date of january 28 2022  filling the lead role of dr michael  morbius is jared leto while he's known  for his sometimes questionable  commitment to his roles we haven't heard  stories of any weird hijinks on the  morbius set just yet what we do know  though is that leto was already a big  fan of vampire stories when he took the  role leto has a long history of  consuming vampire-centered media of  various stripes and has a lot of passion  for the genre from anne rice's interview  with the vampire to bram stoker's  original classic dracula it'll be very  interesting to see how he brings those  influences to the comic book world of  morbius who's a unique vampire character  in his own right i love the opportunity  to do something transformational  arreya rona has been cast as martine  bancroft morbius's fiancee as a  supporting character to the living  vampire who is himself generally not a  leading man it's no surprise that there  isn't exactly a wealth of knowledge  about her to glean from the source  material in the comic stories she often  exists purely to die or be mind  controlled into joining cults giving  morbius sorrow to brood over until she's  resurrected again at one point she also  tried to become a true mythical vampire  and turned on her lover before dying  seemingly for good in this case though  the fact that this lesser-known comic  property doesn't have an expansive lore  could actually work in the project's  favor because it leaves room for a lot  of new invention in the story aro  herself may not be a household name but  she's already got an impressive list of  credits going into morbius you may have  already seen her in shows like true  detective and good omens and films like  pacific rim uprising  matt smith has been cast as the key  villain of morbius his best friend  turned enemy loki's crown who also  suffers from the same blood disease as  the living vampire we don't know much  about the motivations of this character  played by the former time lord but the  disease is fatal so crown certainly has  a lot of desperate motivation to become  the creature morbius is in the comics  crown also goes by the villain name  hunger the character has only appeared  in a few comics but he too is a  pseudo-vampire created by capturing  morbius and experimenting on him to gain  his powers lokis could possibly be a  blend of this villain and morbius's  comics research assistant emil nicos  we'll have to wait and see how the  comics and the films blend on this one  two casting choices from morbius's  supporting characters have piqued our  curiosity tyrese gibson cast as an fbi  agent referred to as agent stroud is  tasked with chasing morbius down in the  wake of his vampiric killing spree then  there's mad men and chernobyl star jared  harris who's been cast as someone  described as morbius's mentor  the first trailer for morbius arrived in  january 2020 with a dark brooding mood  you might expect plus a few interesting  surprises overall the trailer summarizes  morbius's motivation for the film he's  terminally ill and desperate to find a  cure permitting jared leto to get very  broody with the performance hubris is an  underlying theme too with several shots  of morbius receiving awards yet feeling  unsatisfied with the slow progression of  his research that's what drives him to  undertake the absurd steps he does to  cure himself with bats no matter what  his mentor or colleagues say there are a  few intriguing revelations to be found  in the first morbius trailer including a  spider-man easter egg and the return of  michael keaton's vulture but the biggest  surprise might be the revelation that  the source of morbius's vampirism seems  far more mystical than fans perhaps  anticipated he has a weird-looking  ceremonial knife and everything beyond  that we also get glimpses of martine  bancroft who's been upgraded to more  abuse's research assistant for the film  sony pictures describes morbius as a  horror action story about a scientist  trying to cure his own rare blood  disease in the process he accidentally  turns himself into a vampire desperate  for blood he decides to feed on  criminals rather than innocent people in  comics continuity dr michael morbius  attempts to cure his rare blood disease  by inventing a serum distilled from the  vital fluids of bats then hooking up to  an electric line to shock himself as you  might expect this harebrained idea goes  a bit awry and whoops now dr morbius is  a sci-fi vampire that's why he's the  living vampire you see because  science from there morbius's  transformation will make a hero to some  and a villain to others but it's not  clear how he himself will get through it  all  yet at the helm of morbius is daniel  espinoza who was attached at virtually  the same time leto joined the project  his most recognizable director credit in  the united states is for the 2017 alien  horror thriller life but that's not his  only work in his native sweden he  directed the 2010 film easy money and  his other american credits include  safehouse and child 44. on the writing  side of things matsuzama and burke  sharpless handled the script for morbius  after years of working together on other  genre projects their previous credits  include gods of egypt the 2017 power  rangers reboot and dracula untold  we know that morbius is set in the still  developing sony pictures universe of  spider-man supporting characters but  just how much will it connect to the  other spider franchises aside from a  glimpse of horizon labs a fun easter egg  for comics readers who'll recognize the  company where peter parker used to work  the final morbius trailer also makes it  clear that the title character very much  shares a universe with spidey we have an  oscorp sighting affirming that green  goblin norman osborne exists in this mcu  adjacent corner of reality and we also  get another look at whatever's going  down when adrian toombs aka the vulture  meets up with morbius there's also a  daily bugle headline touting morbius's  arrest amid references to other  spider-man characters there's a web of  opportunity this almost certainly only  scratches the surface of what we can  expect in terms of connections between  the various spider-man franchises and we  can't wait to see what's in store  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  superhero movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

